From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Boot into recovery on Kiln OS (issue #47)

Settings > System gets "Boot into recovery" under Restart HelixScreen:
after a confirmation it calls Moonraker's machine.kiln_os.boot_recovery
(Kiln's kiln_os component), whose update agent points the boot flag at
the recovery OS in slot A and reboots. That OS installs an update from a
USB stick or its web page on port 8080. The request goes over the
screen's own connection to Moonraker (127.0.0.1), so it works with the
network down. When the agent refuses (a print is running, start-up has
not finished, slot A doesn't hold the recovery OS), its reason is shown.
The row is greyed while a print is active and shows only on Kiln OS
builds (HELIX_KILN_AD5X). Strings in en and ru.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
